diff --git a/lib/scheduler/kaiair/pktr_dl_power_controller.h b/lib/scheduler/kaiair/pktr_dl_power_controller.h
index 66fc94f95b..4415b3ca7c 100644
--- a/lib/scheduler/kaiair/pktr_dl_power_controller.h
+++ b/lib/scheduler/kaiair/pktr_dl_power_controller.h
@@ -1,25 +1,18 @@
 // SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright (C) 2021-2026 Software Radio Systems Limited
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause-Open-MPI
 //
-// KaiAir / PktR, Tier-A IPC-DL closed-loop power controller (one per UE-per-cell link).
+// KaiAir/PktR Tier-A DL closed-loop power controller, one per UE-per-cell link.
 //
-// On DL the gNB is not the receiver, so it cannot measure per-packet SINR. Instead it drives the
-// per-PDSCH transmit-power offset from the per-packet HARQ-ACK stream, holding the empirical BLER at
-// the PktR target (1 - beta), per-packet reliability P(success) >= beta. The actuator is the
-// pwr_ctrl_offset field (validated on hardware to move real TX power; see dl-power-actuator-confirmed).
+// The gNB cannot measure DL SINR at the receiver, so this loop drives the per-PDSCH transmit
+// power offset from the per-packet HARQ-ACK stream and holds the empirical BLER at the PktR
+// target 1 - beta. The pwr_ctrl_offset actuator was validated on hardware. Boosting clips on
+// this platform, so the offset is a shed-from-ceiling value clamped to 0..15 dB and the loop
+// never goes negative.
 //
-// Authority is one-sided on this platform: boosting clips (the lower-PHY amplitude controller keeps
-// ~12 dB PAPR headroom and PDSCH already sits near the ceiling). So the offset is a SHED-from-ceiling
-// value clamped to [0, 15] dB (0 = max power = ceiling, 15 = -15 dB). The loop adds power by moving
-// toward 0 and sheds by moving toward 15; it never goes negative, so it never clips.
-//
-// Control law (per HARQ-ACK, OLLA-style asymmetric step, converges to BLER = target = 1 - beta):
-//   ack  -> offset += eta * target           (success: shed a little, save power)
-//   nack -> offset -= eta * (1 - target)      (failure: add power)
-// At equilibrium E[delta] = (1-bler)*eta*target - bler*eta*(1-target) = 0  =>  bler = target.
-// The integrator self-smooths, so no separate BLER filter is needed for control (one is kept only
-// for display/debug). This is the measurement-based half of the IPC law; the CQI-based feedforward
-// (set-point) is layered on in a later increment.
+// The control law is an OLLA-style asymmetric step per HARQ-ACK. On ack the offset grows by
+// eta*target (shed a little, save power). On nack it shrinks by eta*(1 - target) (add power).
+// At equilibrium the BLER equals the target. The integrator smooths itself, so the separate
+// BLER filter is kept only for display.
 
 #pragma once
 
